
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:sethost@

%9Parameters:%9

    The parameters are sent to the server as they are; which ones it expects
    depends on the server. The two forms above are the usual ones: a host
    name and a password for normal users, or a user name and a host name
    for IRC operators.

%9Description:%9

    Asks the server to change the host name (and possibly the user name)
    others see for you. Only some IRC servers support this command.

    Since the server usually makes you leave and rejoin your channels when
    your host changes, the channels you are on are first bound to the
    windows they are in, so that they come back in the same windows.

%9Examples:%9

    /SETHOST my.example.org MyHostPassword
    /SETHOST alice staff.example.org

%9See also:%9 OPER, QUOTE, WINDOW

